This was my fourth ascension; the first as a Healer, and the first on
a public server (eos.visi.com).  The Healer was the class I was
playing the first time I made it as far as the Quest (where I got
soundly trounced by the Cyclops), so this ascension has been a long
time coming.  Here are the highlights:

- The entrance to the Mines was behind a secret door on Level 3, so I
ended up doing Sokoban first.  The monsters in the Mines were
suprisingly tougher by the time I went there.

- I still hadn't found a bag of holding after doing Sokoban and the
Mines.  I finally was able to use a magic lamp to get one on DL 12. 
Inventory management is painful without one.

- I nearly died when a watchman had a wand of death in Minetown. 
Luckily I had a wand of sleep, and his first shot missed.

- This was the first time I made my own dragon scale mail.  I wore
white for a long time, then silver after reaching Gehennom (to free up
the amulet slot for life saving [which was never used]).

- The Cyclops is tough.  Really tough.  After he had ONE turn to
attack me, and reduced my HP from ~140 to ~60, I blasted him with a
death ray.

- Though I stayed on my diety's good side until the Astral Plane, I
never got any artifacts from sacrificing (besides the obligatory
Vorpal Blade when crowned).

- After finding the rings of polymorph and poly Control, I made a nice
stack of cockatrice eggs.  Those things are great, except that I
wasted a charge in my wand of wishing because my luck was too low from
breaking eggs!

- I made a potentially fatal mistake while making the eggs: I fell
down a hole while polymorphed (leaving ALL of my stuff behind). 
Luckily I was near the stairs and there weren't any big nasties
waiting for me.

- My second mistake was quaffing an unidentified potion in the Valley
of the Dead.  Of course it was polymorph, and I spent a little time as
a white dragon, and lost my cloak of magic resistance.

- Gehennom was boring as always; luckily I could write enough scrolls
of magic mapping to make it bearable.  One interesting thing: the
entrance to Vlad's tower was in Orcus Town.

- This was the first time I didn't genocide anything (normally I do L,
h, and ;.)  This really made the later game more interesting, and a
lot harder.

- Rodney got a cockatrice egg in the face every time I saw him.  I
don't like messing with him too much.

- The mysterious force wasn't bothering me at all, and I started to
think it wasn't going to be an issue this time.  Then I had to cross
Asmodeus' Lair ten times in a row.

- The Planes weren't too bad.  The Plane of Water is a lot harder when
; haven't been genocided, of course.

- In the Astral Plane, I headed left toward Pestilence, because it
just felt right.  It was right.  I killed Pestilence a few times for
sport, and watched its level steadily going down thanks to the Staff
of Aesculapius.  Then Death showed up, and I decided I'd better
sacrifice the Amulet and get out of there.



